## Improve only where the draft is weak

Use the supplied scene spine and author profile to improve:

- female-centered viewpoint and camera priority;
- microscopic physical state progression instead of broad summaries;
- exact position, direction, pressure, muscular response, internal sensation, secondary body reaction, and aftermath when relevant;
- anatomical honesty, with sensation and interpretation kept distinct from objective fact;
- causal physiology rather than endpoint labels: show where moisture or another established fluid first appears, how it gathers, moves or transfers under contraction, contact, position, rhythm, or gravity, what it changes in friction or sensation, and what residue remains;
- combined Realism and Adult execution: preserve independent choice, genuine difficulty, involuntary reaction, deliberate adjustment or recommitment, proportional change, and consequences without reducing descriptive depth;
- frequent short, character-specific vocal or verbal bursts distributed across the changing action rather than grouped into one block;
- genuine resistance, adjustment, chosen recommitment, limit awareness, or stopping decisions in consensual hard S/M;
- character-specific jealousy, possession, moral contradiction, self-rationalization, and subtle repeated jabs when relevant;
- dialogue-centered realism when characters are conversing: preserve responsive back-and-forth tactics and short private appraisals instead of converting the scene into one long narration or confession;
- tension waves, partial recovery, narrowed stillness or silence, decisive snap, and sustained aftershock;
- declared primary focalization and any bounded secondary female cutaway without private-knowledge leakage;
- removal of generic thoughts, repeated adjectives, invented history, false anatomy, male-centered emphasis, and rushed climax.

Do not lengthen mechanically. Every added sentence must change physical state, perception, voice, choice, tension, or consequence. A quiet beat may remain short when its restraint creates contrast.
